const CATEGORIES={"hosting":["Web hosting and deployment","Compare serverless, static hosting and virtual servers for a new business.","Start with the runtime your code actually needs. A static site may need no server; a persistent process or background job may need a container or VM. Calculate monthly compute, builds, bandwidth, storage and database costs together.","Can the runtime support your code?;Is commercial use allowed on the entry plan?;How are requests, CPU, bandwidth and builds billed?;Can you test rollback and set usage alerts?"],"domains":["Domains, DNS and HTTPS","Compare registrars and the real annual cost of a domain.","A low introductory price is not the same as a low renewal price. Keep control of your domain account and use MFA. Changing registrars is optional; hosting and domain registration can be separated.","Check registration, renewal and transfer price.;Check DNSSEC, TLS and account recovery.;Confirm transfer locks and ownership.;Do not change production DNS before testing."],"database":["Databases for web apps","Compare relational and managed application databases.","Choose a database based on access patterns and the consistency you require, not just free storage. SQLite-compatible databases can work well for small indexed applications; PostgreSQL is useful when existing code and tooling depend on it.","Check supported SQL and data models.;Measure reads, writes, storage and connections.;Review tenant isolation and backups.;Test migration and restore before launch."],"storage":["Object storage and backups","Compare file storage, transfer fees and backup costs.","Object storage is well suited to media and files; it is not automatically a replacement for transactional database queries. Keep private buckets private and account for requests, retrieval and retention.","Estimate GB-months and request counts.;Check transfer and retrieval fees.;Test signed access and private policies.;Restore a sample backup."],"identity":["Authentication and account access","Compare managed identity for customer apps and private dashboards.","Distinguish staff access protection from customer authentication. Decide whether organizations, social login, recovery, session management or MFA are required. Check the provider's definition of active users.","Test authentication and authorization separately.;Estimate active users and SMS costs.;Check recovery and logout.;Verify isolation between accounts."],"payments":["Payments and merchant of record","Compare payment fees, tax handling and checkout responsibilities.","A payment processor and a merchant of record solve different problems. For an eligible software business, a merchant of record may simplify tax obligations but charge different fees. Model effective fees at your actual product price.","Confirm product and country eligibility.;Compare fixed, percentage and subscription fees.;Test payment, refund and cancellation events.;Check payout delays, taxes and dispute terms."],"email":["Transactional email and business inboxes","Compare email delivery services and business mail.","A sending API, an inbound forwarding service and a hosted business inbox are different products. Decide which you need before paying for all three.","Estimate messages per day and month.;Verify sender domain and authentication.;Test inbound replies and bounce handling.;Set sending limits and avoid storing credentials in logs."],"analytics":["Website analytics and SEO tools","Compare traffic measurement, search visibility and performance tools.","Search visibility and website traffic are distinct signals. Begin with the smallest set of measurements needed to decide what to improve. Consider consent, retention, scripts and data processing obligations.","Decide which metrics support business decisions.;Check pageview and site limits.;Review consent and privacy requirements.;Verify tracking on actual pages."],"monitoring":["Uptime monitoring and error tracking","Compare operational monitoring tools for small businesses.","Use external uptime checks for availability and application diagnostics for errors. Logging everything can be expensive and can expose secrets. Prefer measured alerts, sampling and a clear incident process.","Choose critical health endpoints.;Set meaningful alert thresholds.;Estimate event and log volumes.;Test notification and recovery procedures."],"ci":["CI/CD and build automation","Compare repository-based test and deployment pipelines.","A small project can often reuse its existing repository's CI tools. Keep automated deployment permissions separate from code review and use reproducible builds.","Estimate build minutes and artifact retention.;Use scoped secrets and protected branches.;Test failing builds and rollback.;Avoid granting write permissions to untrusted workflows."],"commerce":["Ecommerce storefronts and fulfillment","Compare store platforms, checkout and print-on-demand.","The storefront fee is only one part of the economics. Include product cost, payment fees, shipping, returns, extensions and customer service in your margin calculation.","Estimate gross margin per order.;Check shipping and fulfillment regions.;Test taxes, refunds and delivery.;Verify how order records reconcile with payouts."],"distribution":["App publishing and software distribution","Compare app stores, developer accounts and direct downloads.","Choose a distribution channel based on your target operating system and customer needs. Direct downloads may reduce store dependency but require signing, reliable delivery and secure updates.","Check developer registration and renewal fees.;Verify signing, review and testing rules.;Understand store fees and eligibility.;Test install, update and recovery."],"marketing":["Marketing and advertising platforms","Compare acquisition and email marketing channels.","Validate your audience and conversion path before spending on advertising. For publisher monetization, check content eligibility and privacy obligations. Measure results rather than assuming traffic converts.","Set a maximum acquisition budget.;Check audience and advertising policies.;Use permission-based mailing lists.;Measure conversion and retention."],"support":["Customer support and help desk tools","Compare inboxes and customer-service platforms.","Small businesses can begin with a reliable support inbox and documented response ownership. Consider a help desk when volume or team handoffs justify it.","Estimate contacts, tickets or seats.;Check privacy and data retention.;Define response and escalation ownership.;Test support requests and replies."],"assistants":["AI assistants and source control","Compare tools for planning, development and source management.","A subscription is not equivalent to permission to access a repository, deploy or spend money. Start with manual review and use scoped connections only when needed. Verify actual plan features and limits.","Check commercial use and account limits.;Keep private source and secrets protected.;Verify tool permissions and schedule availability.;Require review before production deployment."]};
const COMPARES=[{"slug":"cloudflare-vs-vercel-vs-netlify","title":"Cloudflare vs Vercel vs Netlify","desc":"Compare hosting for static sites and small web applications, including commercial-use rules and usage costs.","names":["Cloudflare","Vercel","Netlify"],"decision":"For a static business website, compare the commercial terms of each entry plan before choosing. For a Next.js application, check framework features and execution limits. For edge APIs, evaluate runtime compatibility and access to storage. Vercel Hobby is for personal noncommercial projects, so it should not be treated as a free commercial hosting plan.","checks":["Framework and runtime compatibility","Commercial-use eligibility","Build, compute and traffic metering","Rollback and preview support"]},{"slug":"cloudflare-vs-digitalocean-vs-render","title":"Cloudflare vs DigitalOcean vs Render","desc":"Compare edge/serverless hosting, virtual servers and managed web services for a small SaaS.","names":["Cloudflare","DigitalOcean","Render"],"decision":"Use a serverless runtime when your application fits its request-driven execution model. Choose a VM when you need control over persistent processes or system packages, and managed application hosting when you want to reduce server administration. Compare the full cost of persistent storage, backups and databases rather than a headline hosting fee.","checks":["Persistent processes and runtime requirements","Memory and compute limits","Database, backups and bandwidth","Maintenance and deployment ownership"]},{"slug":"stripe-vs-paddle-vs-lemon-squeezy","title":"Stripe vs Paddle vs Lemon Squeezy","desc":"Compare software payment processing, merchant-of-record services and transaction pricing.","names":["Stripe","Paddle","Lemon Squeezy"],"decision":"For low-priced products, fixed transaction charges matter as much as percentage fees. Compare payment processing with merchant-of-record responsibilities instead of treating the products as interchangeable. Eligibility, tax treatment, refund policies and extra subscription fees must be confirmed before making a choice.","checks":["Processor versus merchant-of-record scope","Effective fees at your price point","Refund, payout and dispute policies","Checkout, webhook and entitlement tests"]},{"slug":"d1-vs-supabase-vs-firebase","title":"Cloudflare D1 vs Supabase vs Firebase","desc":"Compare database choices for an early-stage web or mobile application.","names":["Cloudflare D1","Supabase","Firebase"],"decision":"Choose the data model first. D1 is SQLite-compatible, Supabase offers PostgreSQL, and Firebase includes document-oriented and realtime data services. Existing code, query patterns, consistency needs and authorization rules should determine the decision. Do not select a free tier without estimating actual usage.","checks":["Relational versus document data","Existing runtime and client SDKs","Read, write and storage billing","Access policies and restore tests"]},{"slug":"r2-vs-s3-vs-backblaze-b2","title":"Cloudflare R2 vs Amazon S3 vs Backblaze B2","desc":"Compare object storage for downloads, files and backups.","names":["Cloudflare R2","Amazon S3","Backblaze B2"],"decision":"Estimate how much data is stored and downloaded, how often files are accessed, and whether archived data needs fast retrieval. R2 does not charge internet egress from R2, but operation costs still matter. S3 and B2 offer different storage and transfer models; use your actual traffic pattern to calculate costs.","checks":["Storage class and region","Reads, writes and transfer","Private access and retention","Backup restore and portability"]},{"slug":"resend-vs-postmark-vs-sendgrid","title":"Resend vs Postmark vs SendGrid","desc":"Compare transactional email services for application notifications and account emails.","names":["Resend","Postmark","SendGrid"],"decision":"Start by estimating daily and monthly message volume, then check whether you need inbound email processing or marketing campaigns as well as transactional sending. Validate domain verification, bounce handling, rate limits and real delivery in test before selecting a provider.","checks":["Monthly and daily message limits","Transactional versus marketing use","Inbound mail and bounce events","Domain verification and delivery testing"]},{"slug":"shopify-vs-woocommerce-vs-printify","title":"Shopify, WooCommerce and Printify","desc":"Compare hosted stores, self-managed ecommerce and print-on-demand fulfillment.","names":["Shopify","WooCommerce","Printify"],"decision":"These are not all interchangeable: Shopify and WooCommerce provide storefront infrastructure, while Printify primarily supplies print-on-demand fulfillment. They may work together. Build a margin estimate including production, shipping, payment fees, returns, apps and customer support before selecting a store.","checks":["Storefront versus fulfillment responsibilities","Per-order margin","Shipping, returns and tax","Order synchronization and reconciliation"]}];
